## Layering (dbt best practice)

```text
googlesheets.* / kobotoolbox.*
        │
        ▼  staging (views) — rename, cast, light clean; 1:1 with source
stg_googlesheets__* / stg_kobotoolbox__*
        │
        ▼  intermediate (tables) — business logic, spines, cohort assign
int_mentee_database, int_emonc_cohorts, int_emonc_mentees,
int_emonc_mentee_cycles, int_emonc_curriculum_activity_progress,
int_emonc_skill_evaluation_progress
        │
        ▼  marts (tables) — BI contracts
mart_emonc_curriculum_completion
        │
        ▼  metrics (tables) — rolled-up indicators
metric_emonc_curriculum_completion_by_cycle
metric_emonc_cme_coverage_by_cycle
metric_emonc_drill_coverage_by_cycle
metric_emonc_skill_demo_coverage_by_cycle
metric_emonc_return_demo_coverage_by_cycle
metric_emonc_labor_monitoring_coverage_by_cycle
metric_emonc_skill_evaluation_coverage_by_cycle
```

| Layer | Materialization | Rule |
|-------|-----------------|------|
| staging | view | No business filters beyond null/trim; keep raw grain |
| intermediate | table | One clear job per model; reusable across marts |
| marts | table | Stable grain + column names for Power BI |
| metrics | table | Aggregations / rates only — never re-implement mart logic |

## First mart: cohort-aware EmONC curriculum completion

Port of `mentee_curriculum_completion_progress` into layered models.

- **Grain:** one row per `(mentee_id, cycle_id)`, including empty mentee×cycle rows
- **Mentee spine:** EmONC / both from mentee sheets, plus any mentee_id only in facts
- **Skill avg:** AVG of per-skill MAX(average_score) within mentee×cycle
- **Skill assessments:** exclude Partograph (not essential for completion)
- **Cohort 1:** 11 CME, 5 drills, 18 skill demo, 18 return demo, 1 labor, 18 skill eval
- **Cohort 2+:** 13 CME, 5 drills, 20 skill demo, 20 return demo, 1 labor, 20 skill eval
- **date_completed:** first date in cycle when ALL six thresholds met; else NULL
- **Windows:** inclusive on both ends (`cycle_start <= date <= cycle_end`)
- **Add a future cohort:** insert another `UNION ALL` row in `int_emonc_cohorts`

